-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.
--
-- turtle-agent d92d779b (fix/route-order-karazhan_crypt): `plan-export --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --floor-aware
-- --approach-hops --mmaps <the server's mmaps> --rev d92d779b --stamp 20261115030000`. Karazhan Crypt route order fix
-- (issue #1542): the same six bosses in the same order and the same seven legs, 144 packs in walking order and 10 dropped
-- that the walk never wakes; 230 steps against the deployed 270 (313 on a fresh export of the old order), and the walk
-- 6,159 yd against 9,199 (9,076 deployed) for the same 1,900 yd straight route. The dive is the first shaft pack's
-- approach (the deployed dry ramp point, then the shaft floor); the four leg `to` rows are the legs' first packs' own
-- rows. Measurements: ~/TortoiseBots-audit/tests/route-audit-1112/order/karazhan_crypt-FIX.md.

-- karazhan_crypt: map 800, 7 legs, 230 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'karazhan_crypt';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'karazhan_crypt';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'karazhan_crypt';
